  "detailed_description": "Khet Talai Yojana under the Agriculture Department of  Rajasthan Government, The biggest problem for farmers in Rajasthan is water for irrigation. One solution to this problem is a farm pond or in other words, a farm pond, by which the farmer can collect rainwater and use it for irrigation, but all the farmers get it constructed. Therefore, the state government gives a subsidy to the farmers on the construction of farm ponds so that the farmers can collect rainwater and irrigate their fields by making farm ponds in their fields.\n<br>\n\n> **Other important points**\n\n\n1. After the application, administrative approval for the construction of the farm pond will be issued by the Agriculture Department.\n1. Information about this will be received through mobile message/agriculture supervisor.\n1. Spot verification will be done by the department before and after the construction of Khet Talai.\n1. The grant amount will be deposited directly into the farmer&#39;s account.\n\n",
  "eligibility": "\n1. The applicant should be a Farmer.\n1. The applicant should be a native of Rajasthan.\n1. The applicant farmer should have a minimum cultivable land of 0.3 hectares at one place in his name.\n1. In the case of the joint account holder, the minimum land in one place should be 0.5 hectares.\n\n",
